{"toll":{"id":"3e4e3abc-60b9-4822-93d7-8c3cd1c9a33b","word":"toll","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to make the noise of a bell","word":"anunciar"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to make the noise of a bell","word":"badalar"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Martin tolled the great bell every day.","bold_text_offsets":[[7,13]],"type":"example","id":"0cb2e9f1-ab65-42cd-bb01-129162ba346e"},{"text":"Ask not for whom the bell tolls.","bold_text_offsets":[[26,31]],"type":"example","id":"b4c9590f-e320-4fd9-a980-357fcf69b554"},{"text":"From the belfries far and near the funereal deathbell tolled unceasingly while all around the gloomy precincts rolled the ominous warning of a hundred muffled drums punctuated by the hollow booming of pieces of ordnance.","ref":"1922 February, James Joyce, “[[Episode 12: The Cyclops]]”, in Ulysses, Paris: Shakespeare and Company, […], →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[54,60]],"id":"10aacef2-e116-46aa-bf78-2a071a71b09a"}],"senseid":["en:bell"],"categories":["English ergative verbs","English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"raw_glosses":["(ergative) To ring (a bell) slowly and repeatedly."],"glosses":["To ring (a bell) slowly and repeatedly."],"tags":["ergative"],"id":"9735d610-1a22-4d2e-9902-85c08a4467da"},{"examples":[{"text":"The ringer tolled the workers back from the fields for vespers.","bold_text_offsets":[[11,17]],"type":"example","id":"f45eeb33-1735-4f67-a4d0-cbfd162d7eed"},{"text":"When hollow murmurs of their evening bells\nDismiss the sleepy swains, and toll them to their cells.","ref":"1697, Virgil, “The Fourth Book of the Georgics”, in John Dryden, transl., The Works of Virgil: Containing His Pastorals, Georgics, and Æneis. […], London: […] Jacob Tonson, […], →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[74,78]],"id":"f50f8cdd-8671-4253-b6ad-b5c4dc897bcd"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples","English transitive verbs"],"raw_glosses":["(transitive) To summon by ringing a bell."],"glosses":["To summon by ringing a bell."],"tags":["transitive"],"id":"c1f0d5c8-d579-401b-82f0-4bfdf38b1332"},{"examples":[{"text":"The bells tolled the King’s death.","bold_text_offsets":[[10,16]],"type":"example","id":"fc65881a-e44a-48b4-8e4d-8b18f90a0f1a"},{"text":"Slow tolls the village-clock the drowſy hour;\nThe partridge burſts away on whirring wings;\nDeep mourns the turtle in ſequeſter'd bower,\nAnd ſhrill lark carols clear from her aereal tour.","ref":"1771, James Beattie, The Minstrel; or, The Progress of Genius. A Poem. Book the First, London: […] E[dward] & C[harles] Dilly, […]; Edinburgh: A[lexander] Kincaid and W[illiam] Creech; and J[ohn] Bell, […], →OCLC, stanza XLI, page 21:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[5,10]],"id":"7cd86fb5-4730-4982-91d2-1a464a78d1b7"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples","English transitive verbs"],"raw_glosses":["(transitive) To announce by ringing a bell."],"glosses":["To announce by ringing a bell."],"tags":["transitive"],"id":"8c3fca6f-a823-457b-b60f-2de5871ff5fa"},{"examples":[{"text":"The chaplain's first mention of the name Yossarian! had tolled deep in his memory like a portentous gong.","ref":"1961 November 10, Joseph Heller, “Chief White Halfoat”, in Catch-22 […], New York, N.Y.: Simon and Schuster, →OCLC, page 213:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[56,62]],"id":"ca718666-bac8-4d9b-b622-c359105eb33a"}],"raw_glosses":["(figuratively) To make a sound as if made by a bell."],"glosses":["To make a sound as if made by a bell."],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"tags":["figuratively"],"id":"e2bf1f7f-e183-47ec-85ba-f9fad2dcb2c1"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"tolerate":{"id":"bc5face3-66da-41a2-bdf2-18b1b3696886","word":"tolerate","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"To allow without expli